.TH AVR\-VM\-SSH 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-ssh \- Open an SSH session to a RUNNING VM (or print the command with --print).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm ssh
[OPTIONS] CUSTOMER_VM_ID [SSH_ARGS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open an SSH session to a RUNNING VM (or print the command with --print).
.PP
Resolves the VM's SSH endpoint and replaces this process with `ssh`. Extra options are passed through to ssh and placed before the destination, so port-forwarding and similar flags work. Use `--` to stop avr from interpreting them, e.g.:
.PP
avr vm ssh cvm-abc123 -- -L 8080:localhost:80
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fICUSTOMER_VM_ID\fR
\&
.TP
[\fISSH_ARGS...\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIPATH\fR
Private key file to pass to ssh as -i.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the ssh command instead of running it.
.SH SEE ALSO
